WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Sam Rivera: Hi Jordan, thanks for making the time today.

2
00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:11.000
Jordan Lee: Of course. Sorry I'm a bit scattered, we just moved offices this week.

3
00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:18.000
Sam Rivera: No worries, congrats on the move. So the goal today is to agree on the pilot scope.

4
00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:27.000
Jordan Lee: Right. We want to start with the support team only, about twelve people, and see if it cuts response time.

5
00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:33.000
Sam Rivera: That works. We'll go with support only for the pilot, and measure first response time.

6
00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:41.000
Jordan Lee: Great. I'll send over the list of the twelve users by Friday.

7
00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:49.000
Sam Rivera: Perfect. I'll set up the workspace and send login instructions once I have the list.

8
00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:56.000
Jordan Lee: One open question is whether legal needs to review the data agreement. I'll check with them.

9
00:00:56.500 --> 00:01:03.000
Sam Rivera: Sounds good. Internally we were debating discounting the pilot, but let's not get into pricing today.

10
00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:10.000
Jordan Lee: Agreed. Can we meet again on the 14th to review the first week?

11
00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:14.000
Sam Rivera: The 14th at 10am works. I'll send an invite.
